    {
      "id": "6a2d687f4bf8dc7c0291e530",
      "name": "Core Escalation Detection - old",
      "createdByID": 2076840,
      "folderID": null,
      "settings": {},
      "description": "Use this immediately when the customer shows signs of a complaint, refund request, anger, frustration, VIP status, membership dispute, a high-value opportunity ($1,500+), or when 2-3 exchanges have failed to resolve their issue. This playbook hands the conversation to a human.",
      "instructions": [
        {
          "text": [
            "Detect if this conversation needs to be handed to a human and set ",
            {
              "variableID": "6a2c7ca5a0c570b69f38d2c4"
            },
            "  accordingly.\r\n\r\nTrigger if ANY of these are present:\r\n1. Refund request\r\n2. Complaint about service or staff\r\n3. Customer identifies as VIP or long-time/high-value member\r\n4. Membership dispute (billing, contract, cancellation)\r\n5. Opportunity worth $1,500+ (e.g. corporate wellness inquiry)\r\n6. Customer explicitly asks for a human\r\n7. Knowledge base has no answer to the customer's question\r\n8. 2-3 exchanges have passed without resolving the customer's issue\r\n\r\nSteps:\r\n1. Set ",
            {
              "variableID": "6a2c7ca5a0c570b69f38d2c4"
            },
            "  = true.\r\n2. Set ",
            {
              "variableID": "6a2c7c47a0c570b69f38d2bd"
            },
            "  (Standard or High).\r\n3. Tell the customer warmly that you're connecting them with a team member who will follow up shortly.\r\n4. Hand off to WF-VF-04 Escalation Request.\r\n5. Do not continue trying to resolve the issue yourself after escalating.\r\n\r\nDone when: ",
            {
              "variableID": "6a2c7ca5a0c570b69f38d2c4"
            },
            "  = true, customer has been told a team member will follow up, and WF-VF-04 has been triggered."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "pathToolOrder": [],
      "webSearchTool": {
        "enabled": false,
        "messages": null,
        "toolSound": null,
